broad flats of natural salt. Chunks of the hardened stones lay caked
across the ground, some cracked and rising above the surface to form
obstacles through which you must walk. The tall peaks of a large
mountain range prevent travel to the south while ocean waves lap softly
at the coast to the north and west.
