#6759
Salt Flats~
   The vast salt flats of the southern continent lie around you, devoid
of any movement or visible life. Large cracks run across the ground, some
so deep that you cannot even see what lies below. The tall peaks of a large
mountain range prevent travel to the south while the ocean waves lap softly
at the coast to the east.
~
